Subject: [PATCH] locale: a composed launch ignores the operator's shell locale

In the browser process, a composed launch sets LANGUAGE, LC_ALL,
LC_MESSAGES and LANG to the profile's locale before any child process
starts, and resets the C library locale to match. On Linux these
variables decide the application locale, so Intl formatting, the default
calendar and navigator.languages follow --fingerprint-locale, or en-US
when no locale is named. Otherwise a Windows profile launched from a
Thai shell reports Thai formatting and a Buddhist calendar.
--fingerprint=host leaves the environment alone, and
--fingerprint-explain reports the application locale and where it comes
from.

