+  // content/app/content_main.cc runs setlocale(LC_ALL, "") before any embedder
+  // hook exists, so the C library has already adopted the operator's
+  // environment by the time this is reached. glib's application-locale lookup
+  // reads LANGUAGE from the environment live -- which the writes above
+  // therefore do fix -- but falls back to setlocale(LC_MESSAGES, nullptr) when
+  // LANGUAGE is unset, and every other consumer of the C locale keeps the
+  // operator's value regardless. Measured on the shipped linux-x64 artifact's
+  // host: with LANG=en_US.UTF-8 inherited and the composed environment
+  // written, LC_MESSAGES was still en_US.UTF-8.
